<title>GERMANY: Germany's IFO-nearly a million work in environment.</title>
<headline>Germany's IFO-nearly a million work in environment.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH 1996-10-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nearly one million people in Germany make a living from environmental protection, making it almost as many as in vehicle manufacturing, the German economic research institute IFO said on Sunday.</p>
<p>Environmental protection directly employs 508,000 people in Germany, while a further 448,000 are employed in manufacturing goods and services aimed at environmental protection.</p>
<p>Recycling and waste disposal would witness dramatic employment growth in the future, IFO said.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
